LEARNING PASS: direct interaction in the water updates the depth slider
LEARNING PASS: lesson slider supports keyboard adjustment
LEARNING PASS: topic button selects optics controls
LEARNING PASS: air to water at thirty degrees refracts to about twenty-two degrees
LEARNING PASS: air-to-water ray is transmitted
LEARNING PASS: dragging the incident side updates the ray angle
LEARNING PASS: water-to-air ray bends away from the normal
LEARNING PASS: critical angle follows the chosen refractive indices
LEARNING PASS: above the critical angle the diagram shows total internal reflection
LEARNING PASS: lesson headings and live explanations translate into French
LEARNING PASS: language switch preserves experiment settings
LEARNING PASS: returning to a lesson restores experiment state and numeric styling
LEARNING PASS: narrow layout stacks navigation and the pressure-volume graph
